      "description": "Registers where checkout delivers this merchant's events. Webhooks are opt-in: until an enabled endpoint exists for a session's scope, that session's events are still recorded, still readable on the feed, and simply not delivered anywhere.\n**Scope.** An endpoint covers one `(merchant, livemode, account_id)`. `livemode` is the presented key's, never the body's, so a test key can only ever register a test endpoint. Omitting `account_id` registers the merchant's default endpoint, which covers every account with no endpoint of its own; naming one overrides the default for that account alone. A merchant holding a single account registers a default and needs nothing further.\nDelivery resolves the session's own account first and falls back to the default, so adding an account-specific endpoint later re-routes only that account's events and leaves every other account untouched.\nRegistering again for a scope that already has an endpoint **replaces** it, returning `200`; the first registration for a scope returns `201`. Replacement takes effect on the next delivery — events already dispatched for delivery are not recalled.\nThe URL must be `https` outside test mode. A plaintext `http` endpoint would carry a merchant's payment notifications in the clear, and the signature proves provenance without concealing anything.\nAccepts the merchant key only, on the same reasoning as the list.",
